DESCRIPTION:Kwanzaa runs for seven days\, from December 26 through January 
 1\, and is an African American and Pan-African holiday organized around se
 ven principles rather than a single event. Maulana Karenga created it in 1
 966\, which makes it unusual among holidays: its founder is living\, has p
 ublished a book on it\, and maintains an authoritative account of what it 
 is. One thing it is not\, on his own insistence\, is a substitute for Chri
 stmas.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/kwanzaa/
